 Jul 26-29\, with end-of-day AoE deadlines for the 8-page abstract (Feb 1)
 \, full paper (Feb 4) and 2-page extended abstract (Apr 1). Event proposa
 ls (GACs\, community events) are due Mar 18\; a fuller dates page is pend
 ing.\nScope: Cognitive computational neuroscience\, connecting experiment
 s and models of brain computation with artificial intelligence. Character
 istic work compares biological and artificial representations\, models pe
 rception\, cognition and action\, studies neural connectivity and dynamic
 s\, and uses mechanistic interpretability to understand neural-network mo
 dels. The aim is understanding computation and behavior across brains and
  AI systems.\nAdditional topics: Cognitive Science & Computational Cognit
 ion\, Explainability & Interpretability\nScope sources (2027): https://20
 27.ccneuro.org/\nScope last checked: 2026-10-07
URL:https://2027.ccneuro.org/
END:VEVENT
